SUMMARY:NC Arboretum Walk: Gardens\, Trails\, & Paths along a Stream
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nWe will be joining the As
 heville Amblers\, AARP\, Stryder\, and perhaps some others for this walk. 
 The walk is free\, although the Amblers do accept donations (suggested don
 ation: $4.00).\n\nMeet to register inside the Baker Visitor Center at 08:3
 0 a.m. Restrooms are available at the start point. Step-off is at 9:00 a.m
 .\n\nThe walk includes both a guided 5 KM and guided 10 KM option. Both wa
 lks have some moderate hills and stair climbing. A significant part of the
  route is on well-groomed trails with very few obstacles. Some people will
  want walking poles.\n\nWalks are through picturesque gardens\, shaded sce
 nic trails\, and paths along a swift flowing stream. The azaleas should be
  starting to bloom. The trees should be in full greenery and many wild flo
 wers are in bloom.\n\nDress for the weather\; consider a hat and sunscreen
 . Sneakers should be fine\, unless it has rained recently. Be sure to brin
 g plenty of water and a protein snack.\n\nDogs on leash are welcome but ar
 e not allowed in buildings or in the Bonsai Exhibit. Trail strollers shoul
 d be ok.\n\nThe NC Arboretum does not have an admission fee\, but they cha
 rge $25 per car parking fee (so pack as many people in your car as you can
 ). We recommend for the driver to purchase the lowest level annual members
 hip which includes free parking. (Of course\, you may want a higher-level 
 membership\, your choice.) We walk at the Arboretum at least six times per
  year.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/314853375/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260518T224633Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260518T224633Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
